  "details": "As the title describes, I believe that having a independent option to mute chat options from specific players. \n\nI find that the communication is incredibly important, chat being one of them, I find that there's a small disruption when it comes to OSC text. \n\nWhile I find incredible programs that allow users to communicate via text to speech or provide details or achievements such as counters, there's some messages I find disrupting or kind of jarring. Chat Messages such as \"now playing\" or information about their \"pc statistics\" have been starting to be more prolific now that osc is more available to other users. \n\nAt the standpoint of a user I have a few options:\n\n- I could address it to the user to stop projecting it. Which they may or may not comply. \n\n- I could block the user \n\n- I could mute the user removing voice and chat. \n\nNow while I could mute the user I do remove the ability to talk to this individual. While it could be just a chat message, why should it also remove their voice as well? I don't want to turn off chat box for all users as this is used as an accessibility tool but for the few users that I don't want to see the chat box for I would like an independent chat mute option for them. \n\nAdditionally I could see how it can be seen in reverse as well. So I would like to propose these changes: \n\nOriginal moderation actions:\n\nMute: Mute individuals voice and chat box\n\nNew moderation actions:\n\nMute: Mute voice and chat\n\nMute Voice: Mute a users voice \n\nMute Chat: Mute a users chat box",
